Your task is to count the number of ways to construct sum n by throwing a dice one or more times. Each throw produces an outcome between 1 and  6.
For example, if n=3, there are 4 ways:
1+1+1
1+2
2+1
3

Input:
The only input line has an integer n.
Output
Print the number of ways modulo 10^9+7.
Constraints:
1<=n<=10^6

Strategy:
This is very introductory DP. We create an array and populate dp[1] through dp[6] with ones since thats the numbers on a dice. Then we run a for loop 1 through n to go through all the possible sums inside of which we run a loop 1 to 6 to simulate all possible throws. Then we just run dp[i+j]=(dp[i+j]+dp[i])%MOD. For all the nodes and output dp[n].